    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/vocabulary-authority.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Pros and cons, as ruled",
      "prov:value": "Each ruling is the owner's. The reasons are measured against this corpus, not\nread off the specs."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/vocabulary-authority.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "SKOS — **adopted, authoritative for meaning**",
      "prov:value": "| **Pro** | Native JSON-LD. Multilingual labels first-class. `notation` **is** the code — the \"coded glossary\" requirement was already satisfied by `TermGloss`'s prefixed names. Mapping properties with stated equivalence. Carries 135 vocabulary terms + 44 swimlane roles here |"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/vocabulary-authority.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "schema.org — **kept at 3 predicates; never a source of truth**",
      "prov:value": "Owner: *\"i find it hard to find actual definitions/glossary … not sure of\nutility.\"*"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/vocabulary-authority.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Rejected outright",
      "prov:value": "**SKOS-XL** — owner: *\"nah\"*. It reifies labels to fix part of the designation\ngap and nothing else; the gap it does not fix is the one that matters."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/vocabulary-authority.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "DC ↔ SKOS: the overlap, and what stops the drift",
      "prov:value": "They collide only where a node is genuinely both — and one node here is: the\nglossary document is a *file* and a `skos:ConceptScheme`. Measured 2026-09-22,\non output shipped that morning:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/vocabulary-authority.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Guidance for schema and data modelling",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-22: *\"use open standards for modeling. tools can be used to map\nnon-standard/proprietary to standards. first step is data normalization in any\nschema data model mapping exercise.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/vocabulary-authority.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the pins live",
      "prov:value": "It was **undeclared** in `cat-harness.json` until 2026-09-22 — the `dh4f` shape\ninverted, a held directory nothing declares, so every consumer that fans out\nover declared directories skipped it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/vocabulary-authority.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "DC ↔ SKOS: the overlap, and what stops the drift",
      "prov:value": "Two predicates, one fact, nothing declaring which is authoritative. **That is\nthe drift, already live.** The rule above resolves it: the node is a concept\nscheme, so `skos:prefLabel` is the source and `dcterms:title` is the derived\ncopy for resource-metadata consumers. Bean `sl9u`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean sl9u"
      ]
    }
